fs (wasi): copy an imported file in the kernel where it can (homescoop, the KC's install trace)

slicc-kernel >= 1.128.0 has ctx.fs.copyFile: one kernel call per file, no
bytes through the process. copy_file_new (the copy importer, and the
temp file of copy_file_atomic_with_permissions) asks the host for it
through pnpm_fs.copy_file with the mode pnpm computed and O_EXCL; the
kernel applies the umask, doesn't follow a link at the target and removes
a partial target on failure. ENOSYS (an older kernel; asked once) or EXDEV
falls back to pnpm's own open + io::copy.

